  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y={3}^{x}+3.5?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we plot the graph of $y={3}^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/5859dfe6639bc80e8e51681700917fc3a2c9261454b49941d0538d99cb135b6b.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y={3}^{x}+3.5,$ we take the graph of $y={3}^{x}$ and shift it $3.5$ units up. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,4.5),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=3.5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/c8fbb3ffd856b6ecb6f543feb363bba253e7feb695068c0a9dd9c4714616792f.png)",
